From: PickleHik3 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlroots: the Vulkan renderer renders into shm buffers

The X11 backend without DRI3 (termux-x11) takes shm buffers only, and wlroots' Vulkan renderer
only rendered into DMA-BUFs. The renderer now renders into an internal device-local image and
copies each finished frame into the shm buffer the backend presents over MIT-SHM, and
wlr_renderer_autocreate() tries it before pixman, falling back (and logging the choice) when no
GPU renderer starts. Carried as a wlroots patch file that wlroots.wrap applies; the patch's own
header says what it does.
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/subprojects/packagefiles/wlroots/tl/0004-vulkan-render-into-shm.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,690 @@
+Termux Launcher: the Vulkan renderer renders into host (shm) buffers, so the X11 backend can
+present a GPU-rendered frame over MIT-SHM on an X server without DRI3 (termux-x11).
+
+An output that takes shm buffers only (backend buffer_caps has SHM, not DMABUF) and has no DRM
+node gets a renderer from wlr_vk_renderer_create_for_shm_output(): the first hardware (not CPU)
+Vulkan device, with the DMA-BUF format sets not advertised and the formats it renders in optimal
+tiling advertised as shm render formats. For each shm buffer the renderer keeps an internal
+device-local image (the framebuffer renders into it), and the render command buffer copies the
+finished image into a host-visible, cached staging buffer; once the command buffer has completed
+the CPU copies that into the wlr_buffer, which the X11 backend already presents as an xcb shm
+pixmap. No DMA-BUF fence, no foreign-queue ownership transfer and no sync_file semaphore is used
+for such a buffer.
+
+wlr_renderer_autocreate() tries it when the backend has no DRM node and no DMA-BUF, and with
+WLR_RENDERER=vulkan. Automatic selection falls back to pixman when no GPU renderer starts, and
+logs the choice (one INFO line, "Renderer: ..."); WLR_RENDERER=pixman|vulkan forces it.
+Also: a texture destroyed twice before its command buffer completes is queued once.
+
